  // Provide Viewership - regular-only prerequisite the capture does not support.
  // Proof: https://github.com/tarkovtracker-org/tarkov-data-overlay/issues/324
  //        https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Provide_Viewership
  //
  // The 2026-08-27 regular capture carries `AvailableForStart: []` for this task
  // - an explicitly empty list on a present template, which is what licenses
  // `taskRequirements: []` here rather than an absent-from-capture guess. The
  // 1.1-pve capture is identical. Only tarkov.dev's regular record adds Easy
  // Money - Part 2 [PVP ZONE] (66058cb5ae4719735349b9e8).
  //
  // Two things this is NOT resting on. The wiki does document the edge as
  // narrative order - Provide Viewership `|previous = Accept [[Easy Money -
  // Part 2]]`, and Easy Money - Part 2 `|leads to = ... [[Provide
  // Viewership]]`, the "Accept" wording even lining up with upstream's
  // active|complete statuses - so upstream did not invent it from nothing. Per
  // AGENTS.md the infobox `previous` field is narrative order and not proof of
  // an unlock edge, so the empty explicit start-condition list on a present
  // template outranks it; the wiki page has no Requirements section at all.
  // Nor is pve corroboration: the target task is absent from the pve and
  // pvp-season lists entirely, so those modes serving no prerequisite follows
  // from the target not existing there and says nothing about regular.
  //
  // That edge is also the most likely cause of #324: it is the only link from a
  // mode-shared task into the PVP-ZONE Easy Money chain, so a consumer that
  // walks the regular graph surfaces a [PVP ZONE] task for players who never
  // see it.
  '675c15fbf7da9792a4059871': {
    taskRequirements: [], // Was: Easy Money - Part 2 [PVP ZONE] (active, complete)
  },

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Mode-divergent objective maps/counts - tarkov.dev mirrors the PvE text into
  // regular. The wiki (regular witness) documents the
  // PvP variant; the 1.1-pve data carries the other variant. See
  // src/divergences/tasks.json5 for the recorded per-mode counts.
  //
  // Power of Persuasion (63a5cf262964a7488f5243ce) and Easy-Breezy
  // (669fa3a40c828825de06d6a1) used to be corrected here from the wiki. The
  // 2026-08-27 regular client capture shows both objectives byte-identical to
  // PvE (5 kills on Woods/Ground Zero/Ground Zero 21+/Interchange/Customs, and
  // 30 on Reserve/Lighthouse), which is also exactly what tarkov.dev serves for
  // regular - so the overrides were injecting stale pre-1.1 wiki values into a
  // correct upstream record. Removed; see issue #356. The now-redundant
  // divergence records were also retired to git history.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
}
